.TH "CLEAN-DEV-AGENT-CACHES.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clean\-dev\-agent\-caches.sh \- inspect and clear regenerable caches from Podman project homes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBclean\-dev\-agent\-caches.sh --all [--apply]\fR
\fBclean\-dev\-agent\-caches.sh --project NAME [--apply]\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect named rootless Podman volumes of the form
dev-agent-<name>-project-home. Dry-run by default; --apply opts
into removing cache directories only. Other volumes and Docker
storage are out of scope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--all\fR
Inspect all matching project homes.
.TP
\fB--project NAME\fR
Inspect just one normalized lowercase project slug.
.TP
\fB--apply\fR
Delete allowlisted caches. Refuses to run if any rootless Podman
container is running. Never remove named volumes.
.TP
\fB--help\fR
Show usage.
.SH CACHE ALLOWLIST
.nf
.cache/go-build
.cache/pip
.cache/uv
.cache/yarn
.npm/_cacache
.fi
.PP
No complete .cache, .npm, .go, .config, agent-credential or
workspace directories are deleted. Paths with symlinked parents
or targets are skipped. Podman volume mountpoints are validated
against its GraphRoot and commands run through podman unshare.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
clean-dev-agent-caches.sh --all
clean-dev-agent-caches.sh --project gogenmux
clean-dev-agent-caches.sh --project gogenmux --apply
clean-dev-agent-caches.sh --all --apply
sudo btrfs filesystem usage /home
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Run as the ordinary rootless Podman user, not sudo. Stop all
containers before applying. No automatic deletions are performed
at container launch. Interrupted cleanup can leave partly cleared
but regenerable caches. This command does not run Btrfs balance
or remove any Go module downloads.
.SH SEE ALSO
run\-dev\-podman.sh(1), run\-dev\-docker.sh(1)
